# Project — Claude Instructions

## Generated Documents

Write structured output (audits, plans, reviews) as HTML to `claude-docs/`, post a one-paragraph summary + link in chat, tell the user **Alt+D**. Never paste document content into chat.

- `.claude/` — server binary, config, port file (infrastructure only)
- `claude-docs/` — all generated HTML documents and annotations (output/product)

1. Write `claude-docs/<name>-<date>-<HHMMSS>.html` (seconds precision avoids multi-session collisions)
2. `PORT=$(cat .claude/server.port 2>/dev/null || echo 7432)` — set `Alt+D` keybinding to `http://localhost:${PORT}/<name>-<date>-<HHMMSS>.html`
3. Server auto-starts via `Start Claude doc server` VSCode task; manual fallback: `python3 .claude/server.py &`

Every HTML doc must include `<script src="/manifest-link.js"></script>` just before `</body>` (injects Manifest link on left + refresh/timestamp on right of every doc bar; omit only for manifest.html itself). On first use copy `server/manifest-link.js`, `templates/manifest.html` into `claude-docs/`, and download `marked.min.js` into `claude-docs/`:
`curl -s https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@9/marked.min.js -o claude-docs/marked.min.js`

Every HTML doc must include the annotation system from `templates/review-template.html` (CSS + JS verbatim). Four targets, all via relative `/annotations/${DOC}`:
- `.finding`/`.card` divs and `h2`/`h3` headings → `✎ Annotate` button
- Table section rows (single `<td colspan>`) → `✎ Annotate` button
- `<li>` and data `<tr>` items → visible ID badge (e.g. `DG1`) + `✎` icon; keyed by hierarchical heading path

## Confirmation Required

Never implement, edit, create, or commit without first proposing and receiving explicit approval. Proposals are summaries with reference IDs — not exhaustive detail. For larger plans, generate an AUR-style doc and present a screen-fitting summary. Propose → confirm → execute.

A question or problem statement is not a command. Even when the solution is obvious, propose and wait. No exceptions.

## Triggers

**prep session close** — Inventory this session's knowledge not yet promoted to specs; map each item to its target document; find and incorporate any prior unprocessed session-close docs (newer wins on conflicts); generate a merged session-close HTML for review; await explicit confirmation before executing any promotions.

## Project Context

- **Doc server:** port in `.claude/server.port` (default 7432)
- **Keybinding:** `Alt+D` → Simple Browser
- **Spec docs:** All-caps `.md` files are owner's specs — formatting/completeness only, no decisions
- **Updates:** 1–12 words every 15–30 s during long tasks
- **Format:** Short paragraphs, no wall-to-wall prose

